<title>TRINIDAD AND TOBAGO: Conoco executive dies in Trinidad.</title>
<headline>Conoco executive dies in Trinidad.</headline>
<dateline>PORT OF SPAIN, Trinidad 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Joe Vann, a finance manager with DuPont Co's Conoco Inc subsidiary, was found dead in Trinidad this weekend, a company spokeswoman said Monday.</p>
<p>An autopsy was scheduled for Monday in Trinidad, but the spokeswoman said from Houston that his death was believed to have been from natural causes.</p>
<p>Vann, 55, was in Trinidad to establish Conoco Trinidad Ltd. Conoco had announced June 25 that it had been awarded two exploration contrcts for offshore blocks east of the Caribbean nation. The company had said it expected to spend in excess of $50 million to fully evaluate the blocks.</p>
</text>
